ernationally. The company's lifestyle retail chain engages in the sale of western and work-related footwear, apparel and accessories for men, women, and kids. It offers denim, western shirts, cowboy hats, belts and belt buckles, rugged footwear, outerwear, overalls, shirts, safety-toe boots, hats, flame-resistant and high-visibility clothing, and western-style jewelry and accessories, as well as gifts and home merchandise. The company provides its products under the Ariat, Cinch, Cody James, Dan Post, Durango, Horsepower, Idyllwind, Justin, Kimes Ranch, Laredo, Levi's, Miss Me, Montana Silversmiths, Moonshine Spirit, Resistol, Shyanne, Stetson, Tony Lama, Twisted X, Wrangler, Brunt, Carhartt, Cody James Work, Georgia Boot, Hawx, Thorogood, Timberland Pro, Wolverine, Rank 45, Cody James Black 1978, Gibson, Cleo + Wolf, and El Dorado brand names. It sells its products through various e-commerce platform, including websites, mobile app, and third-party marketplaces, as well as retail stores under the Boot Barn brand name. The company was formerly known as WW Top Investment Corporation and changed its name to Boot Barn Holdings, Inc. in June 2014. Boot Barn Holdings, Inc. was founded in 1978 and is based in Irvine, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. John  Hazen | CEO & Director | Age 49 | Compensation: $2.6M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 3K people. Revenue per employee of $593K ranks in the above the sector median among Consumer Cyclical peers, improving at 17%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $33K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $4K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Boot Barn Holdings, Inc. is a mid-cap consumer cyclical business with a $3.9B market cap on $2.3B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +11% over the past three years and +15% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 20% against a 11% cost of capital \u2014 a 9-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat, with gross margins sitting at 33%.","The business throws off $126M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 6 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.35\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 1.3%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 1.6\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 18% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.1776566289275448},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 9.5% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Consumer Cyclical tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Consumer staples outperforming discretionary, signaling cautious spending","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"E-commerce margin compression and tariff exposure \u2014 digital competition erodes pricing power while trade policy reshuffles supply-chain cost structures overnight.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 20% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"How Investors May Respond To Boot Barn Stock After Earnings Guidance Update","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/retail/nyse-boot/boot-barn-holdings/news/how-investors-may-respond-to-boot-barn-stock-after-earnings","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793914202.982,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.178,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance"]},{"title":"BOOT Q3 deep dive: new store expansion offsets slower boot sales and cautious outlook","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/boot-q3-deep-dive-store-032536638.html","date":"2026-11-03","timestamp":1793676336.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.872,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance"]},{"title":"Is Boot Barn Holdings (BOOT) Undervalued After Its 75 To 80 Store Expansion Plan?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/retail/nyse-boot/boot-barn-holdings/news/is-boot-barn-holdings-boot-undervalued-after-its-75-to-80-st","date":"2026-11-01","timestamp":1793561253.969,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.599,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Boot Barn (NYSE:BOOT) R